What is NOT claimed, in four separate levels so nobody conflates them: these drivers build
and link, and their bindings and symbol resolution are verified against the packaged DTB;
that is all.  Nothing is flashed.  No image has been booted - there is no board in this
environment and no emulator either (qemu-system-aarch64 is not installable here, apt has no
package source), so no MMIO write, no translation result, no SMI/LARB state and no boot
log has ever been observed for any patch in this series.  The mkbootimg packaging is
structurally self-consistent (payload- and header-exact round-trip measured in
report/artifacts.json) but is not a flash-ready claim: no ramdisk section, AOSP test AVB
keys, dtbo rev/board-id at packer defaults, and no external source confirms this device's
real boot-partition layout or AVB descriptor expectations.  M4U's and the display client's
function on hardware is untested by definition, and the legacy 32-bit compat ioctls return
ENOTTY because v5.15 carries no compat_alloc_user_space (m4u.c's three compat ioctls are
guarded out rather than faked).

